construction and a completeness account for its declared language. A list of
finished alternatives establishes only their comparison. Where candidates can
be assembled from parts, expose those parts, the sufficiency conditions and the
scope in which the search succeeds exactly when a candidate exists.

Keep the meaning of all compatible contributions separate from the method used
to answer a scoped demand. Prove the method's connection to that complete
meaning, preserve whole contributors and independently required instance
conditions, and execute it on basis sizes relevant to the actual development
problem. A timeout does not establish absence. Candidate construction,
selectivity, semantic correctness and language coverage remain distinct claims.
